ued function $\\mathbf{f}(t)$ is $t \\in [-3,-1)\\cup(-1,\\infty).$" 13194139534551 true] [17592186114836 1100 "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf f(t)$, given by\n$\\mathbf{f} (t) = \\ln{t} \\, \\mathbf{i} + \\frac{1}{t-2} \\, \\mathbf{j} + e^{2t} \\, \\mathbf{k}$." 13194139534551 false] [17592186114836 1100 "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf f(t),$ given by\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{f} (t) = \\ln{t} \\, \\mathbf{i} + \\frac{1}{t-2} \\, \\mathbf{j} + e^{2t} \\, \\mathbf{k}.\n$$" 13194139534551 true] [17592186114836 1145 "To find the domain of $\\mathbf{f}$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\ln{t}$ is $t \\in (0, \\infty)$.\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\dfrac{1}{t-2}$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,2)\\cup(2,\\infty)$.\n- The domain of the 3rd component $e^{2t}$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1737/Source/Images/40ca4990aa765c6a975686a987f4f47c.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{f}(t)$ is $t \\in (0,2)\\cup (2,\\infty)$." 13194139534551 false] [17592186114836 1145 "To find the domain of $\\mathbf{f}$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\ln{t}$ is $t \\in (0, \\infty).$\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $\\dfrac{1}{t-2}$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,2)\\cup(2,\\infty).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $e^{2t}$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/assets/2a4931e8dc80192219736fc4dbc586ad2405bbb628d75bd0e17fa9616567d793.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{f}(t)$ is $t \\in (0,2)\\cup (2,\\infty).$" 13194139534551 true] [17592186114837 1100 "The domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf f (t) = \\tan\\left(t+\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} \\right) \\, \\mathbf i + t^3 \\,\\mathbf j + e^t \\,\\mathbf k$ is\n$t\\in (-\\infty,\\infty), \\quad t \\neq \\bbox[5pt, border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}$.\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139534551 false] [17592186114837 1100 "The domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf f (t) = \\tan\\left(t+\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} \\right) \\, \\mathbf i + t^3 \\,\\mathbf j + e^t \\,\\mathbf k$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty,\\infty), \\quad t \\neq \\bbox[5pt, border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" 13194139534551 true] [17592186114837 1145 "To find the domain of $\\mathbf{f}$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\tan\\left(t+\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} \\right)$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$, except for the values of $t$ for which\n$t+\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} + n\\pi \\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad t = \\dfrac{\\pi}{3} + n\\pi$,\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n- The domain of the 2nd component $t^3$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n- The domain of the 3rd component $e^{t}$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty)$.\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{f}(t)$ is\n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty,\\infty), \\quad t \\neq \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\dfrac{\\pi}{3} + n\\pi}\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." 13194139534551 false] [17592186114837 1145 "To find the domain of $\\mathbf{f}$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of the 1st component $\\tan\\left(t+\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} \\right)$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty),$ except for the values of $t$ for which\n\n$$\nt+\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} = \\dfrac{\\pi}{2} + n\\pi\n\\qquad\\Longrightarrow\\qquad\nt =  \\dfrac{\\pi}{3} + n\\pi ,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer.\n\n- The domain of the 2nd component $t^3$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\n- The domain of the 3rd component $e^{t}$ is $t \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $\\mathbf{f}(t)$ is \n\n$$\nt\\in (-\\infty,\\infty), \\quad t \\neq \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{\\color{blue}\\dfrac{\\pi}{3} + n\\pi},\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is an integer." 13194139534551 true] [17592186115274 1020 #edb/ref 17592186294863 13194139534551 true] [17592186115274 1020 #edb/ref 17592186294870 13194139534551 true] [17592186115274 1020 #edb/ref 17592186294933 13194139534551 true] [17592186115274 1020 #edb/ref 17592186294940 13194139534551 true] [17592186115275 1020 #edb/ref 17592186294856 13194139534551 true] [17592186115275 1020 #edb/ref 17592186294912 13194139534551 true] [17592186115275 1020 #edb/ref 17592186294919 13194139534551 true] [17592186115275 1020 #edb/ref 17592186294926 13194139534551 true] [17592186115276 1020 #edb/ref 17592186294877 13194139534551 true] [17592186115276 1020 #edb/ref 17592186294884 13194139534551 true] [17592186115276 1020 #edb/ref 17592186294891 13194139534551 true] [17592186115276 1020 #edb/ref 17592186294898 13194139534551 true] [17592186115276 1020 #edb/ref 17592186294905 13194139534551 true] [17592186115430 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534551 true] [17592186115430 1100 "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s) = ⟨\\ln (1 + s), \\ln (1 - s), \\frac{1}{1 + s}⟩$." 13194139534551 false] [17592186115430 1100 "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)=⟨\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+s),\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-s),\\,\\frac{1}{1+s}⟩.$" 13194139534551 true] [17592186115430 1145 "To find the domain of $f$, we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components. \n\n- The domain of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+s)$ is $s\\in (-1,\\infty )$ .\n\n- The domain of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1-s)$ is $s\\in (-\\infty ,1).$\n\n- The domain of $\\frac{1}{1+s}$ is  $s\\in (-\\infty ,-1)\\cup (-1,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/assets/3ac2933afc460e42ad5bffb8b01b9fc3ff9275ab3bcf2ac3ab710a8094b36637.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(s)$ is\n\n$\\,$ $s\\in (-1,1).$" 13194139534551 true] [17592186115431 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534551 true] [17592186115431 1100 "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t) = \\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ \\sqrt{2t + 4} \\\\ t^{4} - t^{3}\\end{bmatrix}$." 13194139534551 false] [17592186115431 1100 "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ \\sqrt{2t+4} \\\\ {t}^{4}-{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139534551 true] [17592186115431 1145 "To find the domain of $f,$ we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components. \n\n- The domain of $t$ is $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of $\\sqrt{2t+4}$ is $t\\in [-2,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of ${t}^{4}-{t}^{3}$ is  $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nThe intersection is illustrated in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14033854/assets/d0819fe7e3b82bbf46f6118145903e4dc5640acca4fedf66a734b4d37466e368.png)\n\nTherefore, the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)$ is $t\\in [-2,\\infty ).$" 13194139534551 true] [17592186294856 1017 #edb/ref 17592186294857 13194139534551 true] [17592186294856 1089 "q-160780" 13194139534551 true] [17592186294856 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534551 true] [17592186294856 1100 "Find the domain of the vector-valued function $f(t)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-2)\\,i+\\sqrt{t}\\,j+\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}}\\,k.$" 13194139534551 true] [17592186294856 1113 #uuid "46c8e8de-f68e-51e5-a250-2575f31a97ee" 13194139534551 true] [17592186294856 1145 "To find the domain of $f,$ we need the intersection of the domains of the individual components.\n\n- The domain of $\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t-2)$ is $t\\in (2,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of $\\sqrt{t}$ is $t\\in [0,\\infty ).$\n\n- The domain of $\\frac{1}{{t}^{2}